ls; not a claim old date alone excludes later musicians, nor a different artist as sole boundary. Gurtenfestival names neo-psychedelia and the label explains the distinct revival process. Shared Indonesian psychedelic heritage remains explicit. functionalSong is limited to an authored functional-harmonic verse/refrain realization of these lyric-bearing contemporary pop songs; no measured original harmonic transcription or universal genre form is asserted. Single-coil tremolo guitar with alder body/maple neck and clean strummed articulation, fingerstyle alder dual-single-coil bass, conventional maple kit with traditional cymbals and source-neutral keyboard, synthesizer and unspecified percussion are authored modern choices, not source makes or unreported instrument subtypes. The source explicitly identifies electric-style whammy-bar guitar use. No guessed backing singers or synthesized drums. For the named traditional sound layers, authored large boat-zither with steel strings, modern pop-Sunda repertoire and pelog-degung tuning, Sundanese-context medium kendang with mahogany shell/cowhide heads, and pitched bossed gong struck with a soft mallet preserve the named physical families. Exact subtype, material and technique are candid authored choices, not source session observations. Pelog is expressly mentioned by the artist; no exact scale-frequency transcription is claimed. The sample card does not replace any positively named physical or synthesis role.",
